{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"agent_message","text":"Concurrent streams help when the token dimension is moderate, but large projection GEMMs already occupy the device and contention then costs time. Measurements across the workload set give a clean dispatch rule: parallelize only above about five million attention elements and at most 8,192 tokens. I’m encoding that general size-based rule and separately tuning whether the fused dropout/product pass is worthwhile for small tensors."}}
